      "text_sha256": "7c30e56b67677675384549a428014deb66b28c673869fdef20fc42a18a73dcf5"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "page-0950-block-0013",
      "order": 13,
      "text": "… the voluntary and continuing permission of a patient to be given a particular \ntreatment, based on a sufficient knowledge of the purpose, nature, likely effects and \nrisks of that treatment, including the likelihood of its success and any alternatives to \nit. Permission given under any unfair or undue pressure is not consent.\n",
      "bbox": [
        60.539398193359375,
        271.8770751953125,
        422.81927490234375,
        319.5970764160156
      ],
      "text_sha256": "d3853271f19b2c7866b0bfeb40368392f8821d1d2fce38c8a3bb65d25634d17f"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "page-0950-block-0014",
      "order": 14,
      "text": "For a patient to consent formally they must have the ‘capacity’ to make a decision.\n",
      "bbox": [
        48.039398193359375,
        331.8770751953125,
        403.4393615722656,
        343.5970764160156
      ],
      "text_sha256": "bc8a7ec09c0bb05fc7e56076e3aa2d2c2b4936a0241f2c5a0a2e912376513c70"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "page-0950-block-0015",
      "order": 15,
      "text": "What is capacity?\n",
      "bbox": [
        48.039398193359375,
